{"id": "sllama0041", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Hanukkah menorah has nine candle s. There's one for each night of the festival, plus an additional candle called a shamash that is used to light the others.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0049", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The smallest prime number is two. It is the first prime number in the sequence of primes, which are numbers greater than one that have no divisors other than one and themselves.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0057", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are seven sacraments in Catholic ism. These include Bapt ism, Confirmation, Eucharist, Penance or Reconc iliation, An ointing of the S ick, Holy Orders, and Matrimony.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0065", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Pyrenees run between France and Spain.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0073", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most popular music streaming service is Spotify. It's used by millions of people around the world to listen to songs, create playlists, and discover new music.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0081", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The author of the Diary of a Wim py Kid series is Jeff Kinney. He wrote the books starting with the first one, which came out in 2 007. Each book follows the humorous and rela table adventures of Greg Heffley as he navigates middle school life.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0089", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "James Watson and Francis Crick are credited with discovering the structure of DNA. They proposed the double-hel ix model in 195 3, which showed how DNA carries genetic information.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0097", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for tin is Sn. That' s the abbreviation used on the periodic table.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0105", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The famous book 'P ride and Prejudice' was written by Jane Austen. It's one of her most well-known works, published in 1 813.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0113", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Leonardo DiCaprio played a detective in the movie The Departed.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0121", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Tom Landry won the most Super Bowl rings as a coach, with two.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0129", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The fastest swimmer in the animal kingdom is the sailfish. It can reach speeds of up to 68 miles per hour, making it the quick est creature in the ocean.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0137", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The capital of Mexico is Mexico City.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0145", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Water makes up about 60 percent of your body.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0153", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The animal with the largest eyes in the world is the colossal squ id. These giant eyes can reach up to about 1 0 inches across, which is roughly the size of a dinner plate. They help the squ id detect light and predators in the deep ocean where it lives.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0161", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The capital of South Korea is Se oul.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0169", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are 6 0 minutes in an hour.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0177", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Torah contains a total of 6 1 3 commandments, known as mit zvot. These are divided into two categories: positive commandments, which require action, and negative commandments, which prohibit certain actions. They are spread throughout the first five books of the Torah, covering spiritual, moral, and practical aspects of Jewish life.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0185", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The city known as the \"City of Canals\" is Ven ice, Italy.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0193", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for silicon is Si.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0201", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The currency used in India is the Indian Rupee. It is denoted by the symbol IN R or Rs., and it' s divided into hundred paise, though paise are no longer commonly used in daily transactions.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0209", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The capital of India is New Delhi.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0217", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Nigeria has the largest population of any African country. It' s a really big place with lots of people living there.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0225", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Joseph St alin was the leader of the Soviet Union during World War II. He became the leader in 19 22 and stayed until his death in 1 9 53. During the war, he led the country through some of its most difficult times, especially when Germany attacked in 1 9 41. His leadership was crucial in turning the tide against the Axis powers.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0233", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The currency used in Japan is the Japanese y en, often abbreviated as JPY. It's the official money of the country, and you' ll see it on bills and coins when you visit or shop there.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0241", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest land ma mmal on Earth is the African elephant. They can weigh up to six or seven tons and stand about 1 0 feet tall at the shoulder.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0249", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The capital of Greenland is Nu uk. It's a beautiful city located on the northern coast, surrounded by stunning landscapes and icy water s. N uuk serves as both the political and cultural center of the country, offering insight s into Green land's unique heritage and way of life.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
